rting from floodplain agriculture  to to wetland conservation the  restoration costs and the management  cost of those protected areas not huge  if you put that together benefits  outweigh costs  I suppose the the main point here that  was of interest to the company is to be  able to say that they are delivering  value that it's measurable economic  value it's greater than the costs that  they are incurring themselves or that  they are imposing on the agricultural  producers and that this although they  can't cash in they can't turn that value  into cash flow for the company there  nevertheless making a positive  contribution to the economy of the area  in terms of these environmental benefits  so just some some brief thoughts on what  they concluded from this the values of  wetland restoration and creation are  significant the costs are relatively  small as you'd expect the net benefits  our greatest where the opportunity costs  are lower and they were most excited  about the possibility to integrate this  valuation approach into their existing  procedures most like most companies they  have very elaborate procedures for  environmental and social impact  assessment yes  ESI a which typically do not include any  kind of economic valuation so they were  looking at this as  a test case a pilot to use valuation  build that into their environmental and  social impact assessment to try and  deliver better decisions on how to use  restoration resources okay what I've  tried to do and I realize we've still  got some time ahead of us briefly wanted  to look at what's the business case why  should business care about biodiversity  ecosystems what are the drivers of those  of changes in interests how do we  understand the linkages positive and  negative and dependence between business  and biodiversity and I looked at a case  study example what I'm proposing to do  next week is to look at the next  sequence of chapters in the the teeb for  business report looking at what kind of  things can business do to avoid or  mitigate biodiversity risks what are the  new business opportunities in  biodiversity and ecosystems and then  lastly how do we get what can we expect  business to do on their own on a  voluntary basis and what requires  government action to try and tighten up  the the rules that they they work on how  do we change the incentives this is a  slide you've all seen before I took the  liberty of adding some additional logos  these are the different organizations  that contributed to the teep for  Business Report I will stop there  briefly and I realize we've got some  time still about 10 10 15 minutes yeah
 

